-- A thread is about a post or a photo, and so is each comment in it. The condition tests the
-- thread's own `target`, and then, inside the filter over the thread's comments, reads `body` on
-- each comment's `target`.
--
-- The compiler accepts it. Inside the filter a bare `target` is the comment's, which no test has
-- shown to be a Post. A thread about a post with a comment about a photo makes the running system
-- fail when it reads the condition: "'body' is not readable on 'Photo' instance".
-- `PathResolutionDisagreementTest`, "a test on the subject is taken to hold for a field of the same
-- name on a filter's record", pins both.
act Post { body: text }

act Photo { caption: text }

shape Content = Post or Photo

act Thread { target: one Content }

act Comment {
    target: one Content
    thread: one Thread
}

shape ThreadWithEmptyComment = Thread where target is Post and exists (comments where target.body == "")
